Holotone Public includes an AGPL-compatible runtime wrapper around hydra-synth
(host creation, media binding helpers, dual-canvas / iframe embed surfaces, and
the postMessage protocol used by the private StrangeLoop instrument).

Corresponding Source
--------------------

If you interact with a deployed instance of this site (including iframe embeds),
AGPL §13 requires an opportunity to obtain Corresponding Source for the version
you are using. The canonical Source offer is:

  https://github.com/MartinScriblerus/holotone_public

A visible “Source” link is also rendered on embed and projection surfaces.

Relationship to StrangeLoop
---------------------------

StrangeLoop (private) owns ChucK / WebChucK audio, MIDI, and instrument UI.
It must not import hydra-synth. It may embed this site via iframe or open a
projection window and exchange LiveProjectionSnapshot-compatible messages.

This separation keeps the AGPL covered work limited to the visual / Hydra lane
and this public documentation surface.
